  "id": "DrugBank_DB01598 - MONDO_5972",
  "verbalization": "Imipenem, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Streptococcal Pneumonia through a series of off-label and indicated uses that suggest a potential mechanistic link. The evidence points to Imipenem being used off-label for Campylobacter Fetus Infectious Disease and Subacute Bacterial Endocarditis, both of which are associated with Cilastatin, a drug that is indicated for Streptococcal Pneumonia. This suggests a possible indirect pathway where Imipenem may influence the microbiome or immune response in ways that could contribute to the development of pneumonia. The presence of Cilastatin in the chain indicates a possible role in modulating bacterial activity or inflammatory responses, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of drug–disease relationships and the need for further mechanistic investigation to establish a direct causal link.",
